{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAFtk5GmxdP3coMpvvHc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it in `recovery.go`. When a handler panics with `http.ErrAbortHandler`, the recovery middleware now handles it the way it handles a broken pipe. It logs one line instead of a stack trace, records the error on the context and aborts. It no longer calls the 500 recovery handler. The check uses `errors.Is`, so it also catches the error when it's wrapped.\n\nI added `TestPanicWithAbortHandler` in `recovery_test.go`. It fails without the fix and passes with it (GATE PASS), and the format, whitespace and debug-leftover checks were clean.\n\nI only ran the `TestPanic*` tests, not the full suite. The change isn't committed yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1192,"cache_read_input_tokens":34644,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1192,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c33149e-e0aa-4659-b8a9-f7c445db56e3","uuid":"34b1c87f-73e7-4b6b-b4a6-67cb5d99fd72","timestamp":"2026-10-18T19:30:35.078Z","request_id":"req_011CgAFtjqPH12rwwEV42z7T"}
